  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/... \n\nGradually warming temperatures and overall tranquil weather is\nexpected through at least the first half of the next workweek with\nquasi-zonal flow in the wake of the weekend low. An increase in H5\nheights up to 579-582 dam by Monday will support the gradual\nwarming of temperatures, with afternoon highs reaching the middle\n80s and lows in the upper 50s to lower 60s across the lower\ndeserts, which is right around normal for the time of year. Dry \nmostly clear skies will prevail under this pattern as well. Model \nuncertainty grows later next week as there are hints at some \nmoisture return into the region from the southeast, then a \npotential atmospheric river approaching by next weekend. Either, \nor both of these moisture sources may eventually help to bring a \nreturn to rain chances at some point before the end of the month, \nbut it is too early to have a good idea on timing and/or placement\nfor any weather feature this far in advance.",
